  "version": "0.8.0",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.7.1`\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\n- **Nested connection groups.** Groups can hold other groups; the connections panel shows them as a tree, and Settings → Groups adds search and dragging several ticked connections at once.\r\n- **Faster over slow links.** Typing shows locally before the remote echo returns, and a new compose bar sends a whole command at once, runs pasted lines one at a time, sends to broadcast targets and suggests from history.\r\n- **Jump hosts.** A hop can log in as a saved connection, and a hop or tab that is already connected is reused instead of logging in again.\r\n- **~/.ssh/config, read the way ssh reads it.** Wildcard `Host` and `Match` blocks, per-hop `ProxyJump` blocks, `Include` paths, `%` tokens and `${VAR}` in `IdentityFile`/`CertificateFile`, plus OpenSSH's `known_hosts` files (including `UserKnownHostsFile`/`GlobalKnownHostsFile`).\r\n- **Local shells.** Settings → Local shells keeps your own shells with arguments, lists each WSL distribution, and Auto picks PowerShell on Windows. A shell that fails to start shows why and lets you fix it in place.\r\n- **System integration.** A `tterm` command (`tterm .`) and \"Open in tTerm\" in the file manager's folder menu, removed again on uninstall.\r\n- **SFTP.** Open remote files in a local program (with Open With), work as root through sudo, and see large downloads progress.\r\n- **Also:** settings search, AI agent and shell logos on tabs, AI agent hooks installed on SSH servers, `COLORTERM=truecolor` sent to SSH servers.\r\n\r\n## Before you upgrade\r\n\r\n- **Upgrade every device that syncs together.** Nested groups change the sync and backup format; tTerm 0.7.x cannot read data written by 0.8.0.\r\n- **No downgrade.** The local database is migrated on first start and 0.7.x cannot open it afterwards.\r\n- **New defaults:** shell integration is on for SSH sessions and macOS local shells; terminal tab content is restored after a restart; right click pastes on Windows; tab and search shortcuts follow each platform's convention.\r\n\r\n## Known issues\r\n\r\n- With blur on, small white wedges can show at the window corners.\r\n- SFTP follow-terminal does not work in tmux or with macOS's built-in `/bin/bash` (3.2).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n**Full comparison:** [v0.7.1...v0.8.0](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.7.1...v0.8.0)\n",
